  (`pm1_<stem>`) its "behind PM-1, F1+D2b" functions over mirrors of their bodies (aterm
  docs/PLAN-tests-to-specs-2026-10-15.md), fieldless enums by value. Each `blob_<stem>` is the
  stage-2 compiler's artifact of `blobs/d2b_rows/<stem>.rs`: aterm functions copied verbatim
  with their SPEC HARNESSES (the body, then the crate's SPECS.md clause written apart from
  it; `ok as u8 - 1` underflows exactly when the clause is false). A row is
  `RowProvedB3`: its harness never panics on any valid input, so the clause holds for every
  input, and B3 binds every enum of the artifact to rustc's own discriminants
  (`b3probe.rs`, `b3_rustc.tsv`). Per artifact: the certificates perturbed (`refused_cert_*`)
  and B3 over a swapped table refused (`b3all_refused_*`); per row: a FALSE clause's harness
  unsafe at a named counterexample (`*_wrong_unsafe`), the row's own harness valid at that
  input (`*_cex_valid`) and clean there (`*_spec_runs_at_cex`). Then VF7's `creation_flags`
  row carried over to `RowProvedB3`.
-/
